AB  - To expand our understanding of male homosexual attraction, we analyzed homosexual written graffiti (N = 406)from two men's restrooms. Eighty-three percent of the graffiti had contact-seeking content. The most frequently desired object traits were male genital traits, which comprised 36% of all desired traits. In sexual exchange, the most frequently desired behaviors were oral (33%) and anal (25%) behaviors, while sadomasochism comprised 13% of all desired behaviors. Most contact-seeking messages that did state a role preference, expressed that subjects desired a submissive-recipient role in sexual exchange. The submissive-recipient role was most markedly desired in sadomasochism, which supports those earlier studies that have found homosexual masochists to outnumber homosexual sadists.
