TI  - Snatch Theft Detection using Low Level Features
AU  - Ibrahim, Norazlin
AU  - Mokri, Ss
AU  - Siong, Ly
AU  - Mustafa, Mm
T2  - Doaj.Org
AB  - In practice it is difficult to diagnose events based on the ability to segment the individual persons in a crowd.. The used of low level features is seemed to be more effective to identify the abnormality situation. This paper presents the detection of snatch theft in pedestrian crowd movement. It is based on the features extracted from the computation of optical flow for sequence of video frame. Kalman filter is used to detect the start and the end of of possible snatching events. The event is classified based on the distribution of the optical flow vectors before and after the events using vector matching and SVM classification. The algorithm has been tested on simulated events, and showed a good detection rate of snatch theft events..
