AB  - These findings are from a study of burg l a ry investigation conducted in three policing are a s : O x f o rd, Chiltern Vale and Coventry. The study emerged from Home Office evaluations of b u rg l a ry Strategic Development Projects in the three sites, which were funded by the Home O ffice and evaluated by a consortium led by South Bank University. The three sites were selected for the study on the grounds that a major element of each of the Strategic Development P rojects was the enhancement of police perf o rmance in the investigation of burg l a ry. Key points • The investigation of burglary should not be characterised as a simple, step-by-step process. Rather, the process of investigation should be understood to be complex, dynamic and multi-layered.
