AB  - The Handbook on Crime is a comprehensive edited volume that contains analysis and explanation of the nature, extent, patterns and causes of over 40 different forms of crime, in each case drawing attention to key contemporary debates and social and criminal justice responses to them. It also challenges many popular and official conceptions of crime. pt. 1. 'Conventional' property crime -- pt. 2. Fraud and fakes -- pt. 3. Violent crime -- pt. 4. Sex-related crime -- pt. 5. Drug-related crime -- pt. 6. Organised and business crime -- pt. 7. State, political and war crimes -- pt. 8. Harms, health and safety.
