AB  - This chapter examines the particularities of a sonorous urbatext, focusing on sound and materiality in the first slam album of Grand Corps Malade, Midi 20. Two repeated words provide the key to the urbatextual analysis in this album. Grave(r) evokes the physical act of writing in order to leave a textual mark on Seine-Saint-Denis, and coup expresses the sonic power words can perform on the listener. Emulating graffiti artists and canonical poets, Grand Corps Malade creates geopoetic landscapes to highlight the problems in the Parisian suburbs, which allow him to develop a technique of intertextuality and appropriation of the urban peripheries.
