AB  - Based on current empirical data from a nationwide survey of children, adolescents and their parents conducted by the German Youth Institute (DJI) the article addresses the subject offender-victim relationships. It thereby focuses on experiences of physical violence of juveniles, as victim, offender or both. The paper uses a theoretical model, which refers to the Situational Action Theory, the Routine Activity Approach and concepts of risk and protective factors. From this model the probabilities for victimization and/or own delinquent action are derived and empirically tested.
