AU  - Albers, S
AU  - Feltes, T
AU  - Ruch, A
T2  - MONATSSCHRIFT FUR KRIMINOLOGIE UND STRAFRECHTSREFORM
AB  - The analysis was based on the German Federal Central Criminal Register (BZR) data of all persons affected by a national stadium ban in March 2012. Thus, it investigates the question whether the association linked with a stadium ban, that football fans posing an increased safety-risk, goes along with an increase of registrations in the Federal Central Criminal Register. As a result, a high amount of criminal sanctions can be detected, which persists throughout all age groups. In addition to violent offences, strikingly high amounts of verbal insults, resistance against enforcement officers, trespass and riots can be observed. Explanatory approaches for the results include lifestyle and routine activities as well as the consequences of judicial selection mechanisms. The article concludes with recommendations for the handling of football fans ready to use violence.
