TI  - Socio-Spatial Crime Prevention Validation of the ISAN Prevention Model in Two Housing Estates
AU  - Schubert, H
AU  - Veil, K
T2  - MONATSSCHRIFT FUR KRIMINOLOGIE UND STRAFRECHTSREFORM
AB  - This article describes the explorative validation of the ISAN model of prevention using a causal steps mediation analysis on the basis of a household survey conducted in two German housing estates. The ISAN model was developed as a structural framework that integrates different levels of crime prevention in a socio-spatial context. It contains three approaches and theoretical concepts of crime and prevention: (a) primary prevention through social policies, (b) situational crime prevention and (c) social ecological prevention and community building. The framework distinguishes between levels of operation and less between theories of prevention. The model will be introduced in the first part of the article on the basis of socio-spatial theories of crime and prevention and then be empirically explored in the second part. The research is based on a face-to-face survey. The results provide an integrated perspective on environmental criminology that widens the perspective of situational prevention and defensible space.
