TY  - JOUR
TI  - Gardener in a troubled Eden
AU  - Abedi-Lartey, M.
AU  - Holden, J.
T2  - Africa Geographic
AB  - Describes the experiences of the author, a Fauna & Flora International (FFI) programme manager, working in Liberia's wild and beautiful Sapo National Park. States that it is not easy being a champion of wildlife in a country where recent civil war resulted in its inhabitants rather looking at their own survival than that of their environment. Explains that the FFI programme focuses on supporting Sapo authorities in their efforts to monitor and protect the forest and its biodiversity, while also assisting the local communities to benefit from the park. Mentions the FFI runs awareness-raising initiatives to gather support for Sapo's conservation, helping the local people to develop ways of making a living without harming this rainforest and its wildlife. Comments on the development projects funded by other environmental and development agencies, such as the construction of schools, and clinics, supplying hand-pumps and ventilated pit latrines. Emphasises six of these park-fringe communities also benefit with livelihood support programmes that focus on tending gardens, raising livestock, soap-making and communal forestry. Warns however of this pristine haven constantly being threatened by illegal hunters and alluvial gold-miners, at least 15 active camps in the region
