TY  - JOUR
TI  - Ban hunting. Part 1
AU  - Cheney, C.
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - Emphasises that there is a powerful force behind the movement to ban hunting in all its forms and warns against ignoring this threat. Stresses the importance of hunting as a pragmatic and rational form of wildlife management and sustainable utilisation of a renewable natural resource. Attempts to expose the motives of animal rights groups, also their complete misunderstanding of the natural order and realities of Africa. States that the animal rights movement is by far the biggest danger to wildlife, because if excess wild animals are not managed with either translocation, culling or hunting, they will increase until populations begin to impact negatively on the environment. Warns also of habitat loss, as most forms of land use, whether agriculture or ecotourism will consume wildland habitat without which wild animals cannot exist. Defines some concepts, namely utilitarian value, consumptive use, non-consumptive use and sustainable utilisation. Looks at four questions involving wildlife and wildland use, including justification of not utilising natural resources by legal means, as illegal hunting and poaching has not decreased by the banning of legal trade and hunting, States thus wildland will be put to alternative use and therefore lost of species could occur
