TI  - EDO TORI DON'YA NO GOYO TO CHORUI RYUTSU KOZO.
AU  - Yasuda, Hiroko
T2  - Bird wholesalers in Edo and their distribution network.
AB  - Discusses the distribution network of Edo-based bird wholesalers and their responses to the changing business environment toward the end of Tokugawa shogunate period. The bird wholesalers supplied hawking bate as well as waterfowl. Their number was restricted after 1725, and they monopolized the market thereafter, but they were also obliged to make contributions to the shogunal government. With the opening of the port of Yokohama, the wholesalers saw a rise in demand for fowl, but they also faced increased illegal hunting and later experienced a hawking ban.
