TI  - Around Africa: Caught on camera; Africa at a glance
AU  - Portmann, F.
AU  - Anon
T2  - Africa Geographic
AB  - Illustrates by a photograph how a black-backed jackal sneaked between the huge legs of an elephant to slake its thirst at the Nebrowni waterhole in Etosha National Park. Briefly discusses the negative influence of climate change on South Africa's groundwater resources, researchers recommending monitoring patterns of use. Looks at a joint operation between SANParks and the police when arresting eleven suspects in connection with rhino poaching and illegal trading of rhino horn. Points out that southern Africa is a botanist's dream, such as the daisy family, Asteraceae with prolific numbers in all Africa's biomes. Comments shortly on the release of three brown hyaenas, Hyaenia brunnea, in the Mountain Zebra National Park and also the approval of a controversial building development next to Kamfers Dam in Kimberley, housing the biggest population of lesser flamingos in the country. Refers to elephant and Grevy's zebra numbers increasing in northern Kenya, according to the latest 2008 count. Briefly mentions an expedition of UK scientists to the Mozambique Mount Mabu forest to identify areas for conservation, and world's conservation organisations declaring 2009 as Year of the Gorilla, with permission of the rebel leader to see them in the Congo
