TY  - JOUR
TI  - Die wildplaasbestuurder - wie is hy?
AU  - Van der Walt, R.
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - States as the result of the development in the wildlife industry not only did the relationship between hunter and landowner change, but also demanded that both should regard the role that the game ranch or farm manager plays with new eyes. Points out that traditionally the landowner appointed a foreman to handle his farm and when the owner changed from livestock and crop farming to game ranching, the foreman stayed on without the necessary training and experience of the game industry. Emphasises that currently game ranch managers are formally trained with relevant tertiary qualifications and contributing to the scientific and successful management of game farms. Describes the number of responsibilities that rest on the shoulders of game ranch managers, such as ecological advisor, training and supervising employees, determining the quota of game to be sold or hunted, knowledge of wildlife legislation, marketing and catering. Mentions also regular inspection of slaughtering facilities, maintenance of game fences, roads and water supply and the making firebreaks. Comments on the added responsibility of protecting the farm against illegal hunters and illegal immigrants
