TY  - JOUR
TI  - When protection falters.
AU  - Caro, Tim
AU  - Scholte, Paul
T2  - African Journal of Ecology
AB  - The article comments on the decline of large mammals, specifically antelopes, in many African national parks. The natural and anthropogenic causes of the herbivore population declines include illegal hunting, drought, poaching, population growth, immigration and demands for a higher standard of living. Factors that promote bush meat consumption are also discussed. Setting aside large tracts of land in remote areas far from human populations is a viable conservation option in some parts of Africa, but this approach is increasingly outmoded by land-use change, demographics and policy reform. A faunal relaxation in Africa's network of reserves is an option that could leave a continent containing isolated pockets of large mammals diversity living at low population sizes.
