TY  - JOUR
TI  - Poaching epidemic
AU  - Coetzee, M.
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - States that many people watching the actuality programme on television, Carte Blanche in October 2009 probably had doubts on the ability of the South African government to protect property owners against attacks by land-hungry people. Mentions that Carte Blanche also screened a programme in August 2008 on the bushmeat trade, to highlight the rampart poaching of animals on game ranches in the Hoedspruit area. Emphasises since then reports from other parts of the country have been received concerning increasing of poaching. Warns animals are the legal property of landowners, while there is a perception of landless people to being deprived of access to meat of game animals, as they feel they have the traditional right to poach the game for food. Mentions the other side of poaching is purely for financial gain, such as the killing of especially white rhinos and the participation of crime syndicates. Explains this culture of a `free for all' could be the result of a situation where the citizens were promised land they did not receive, thus forcing legitimate owners off their land by any means, including poaching of game for food. Warns of the serious threat to wildlife conservation and include colour photographs to illustrate the carnage left by the poachers
