TI  - Illegal hunting continues in Malta
AU  - Anon, A
T2  - Birdwatch Magazine
AB  - BIRDS Abstract: This year’s  ‘Raptor Camp’, organised by BirdLife Malta, has been assessing the population of migrating birds and witnessing and recording the slaughter over the last two weeks. The RSPB’s Grahame Madge, who attended the Raptor Camp,said: “To anyone who hasn’t seen it for themselves, the scale of the slaughter beggars belief. “On good days for migration, when several hundred birds of prey pass through, the hunters are stirred into a frenzy – desperate to shoot as many as possible, even within protected areas. On one day, I witnessed a large movement of Honey Buzzards and other birds of prey. The hunters could clearly be seen identifying the best vantage points in a bid to shoot them.”
