TY  - JOUR
TI  - Africa at a glance: around Africa
AU  - Anon
T2  - Africa Geographic
AB  - Discusses briefly issues regarding conservation of wildlife and ecology. States the level of rhino poaching and killings increased sharply in East and southern Africa during 2009 on private ranches and national parks. Looks at the anti-poaching operations taking place in Kenya, Zimbabwe and South Africa. Mentions the use of weevils (Cyrtobagus salviniae) of Brazil, to eradicate Kariba weed threatening fishing and tourism in the Okavango Delta of Boswana, as this aquatic fern suffocates fish by cutting off its oxygen supply. Relates of the parasite causing malignant malaria in humans (Plasmodium falciparum) recently discovered in the gorillas of Cameroon. Warns the destruction of their forest habitat will lead to more contact with humans, thus causing pathogen transmission. Comments on Somali pirates operating on the East Coast keeping illegal fishing trawlers away, thus barracuda and red snapper have returned and Kenyan fishermen now have larger catches. Regrets Tana River Delta is under siege again of developers who were stopped in 2007 but in 2009 Kenya's High Court ruled in their favour although this wetland is important for migratory birds. Mentions an Australian company given permission for opencast coal mining in Tete Province, Mozambique
