TY  - JOUR
TI  - Africa at a glance
AU  - Anon
T2  - Africa Geographic
AB  - Briefly discusses some conservation issues regarding Africa. States that chimpanzees of the rainforests of Guinea have learned how to recognise the snares laid by hunters, even intentionally setting them off without being harmed. Looks at the moving of wild animals to the new enlarged area of Addo Elephant National Park after the removal of a boundary fence that previously separated the two sections. Reports on a filter that purifies water poured from a bottle and developed by researchers at Stellenbosch University. Explains a bag, like a tea bag, inside a tube that is fitted onto a bottle, contains carbon that removes harmful bacteria and chemicals from the water. Mentions an oil spill of some 100 tonnes of diesel fuel into the Nile River in southern Egypt after a barge sank near Aswan and the recent arrest of nine people, including two veterinarians, from Modimolle in connection with the poaching of rhinos. Focuses on the discovery of a possible new giant elephant-shrew species in coastal Boni-Dodori forest of Kenya. Describes the joint effort in the DRC for solution of land conflict threatening the Virunga National Park, affecting refugees and wildlife. Warns of freshwater species of Africa threatened by extinction due to agriculture, water usage, dams and invasive species
