AB  - BIRDS Abstract: A new BirdLife campaign is up and running, helping to explain the importance of migration and stop illegal hunting in southern Europe. For migratory birds, illegal killing is an additional threat to their already dangerous and challenging journey. The EU Bird Directive protects the millions of birds who travel between their nesting and wintering grounds twice every year, by stating that only a few species can be hunted under certain conditions of timing and methods. In the Mediterranean, violations of EU legislation are particularly widespread, exacerbating the substantial decrease in migratory bird populations over the past 40 years
