TY  - JOUR
TI  - Watch Out, Bullwinkle!
AU  - Neale, Todd
T2  - Audubon
AB  - The article focuses on the effort of Nova Scotia's Department of Natural Resources (DNR) to combat illegal hunting of the endangered moose population on the mainland part of the province. Bullwinkle is a life-size moose replica made from a durable lightweight and inexpensive Styrofoam material. The decoy is used by conservation officials to caught poachers. According to John Mombourquette, enforcement director of the DNR,  illegal harvesting was viewed by conservation officials as a major limiting factor on the recovery of mainland moose. Poachers will face fines and six months in jail if convicted.
