TI  - First hand-reared Spoon-billed Sandpiper returns to breed
AU  - Anon
T2  - Bird Watch
AB  - BIRDS Abstract: The first hand-reared Spoon-billed Sandpiper has returned to breed in Chukotka, Russia, where it was hatched two years ago. The species, which is unique in the animal kingdom for being born with a spoon-shaped beak, has witnessed its numbers decline by a quarter year-on-year, and it is likely that fewer than 100 pairs remain in the wild. WWT aviculturist Roland Digby has reared 24 Spoon-billed Sandpipers over the last two summers on their breeding grounds in north-eastern Russia, giving them a head start to ensure they survived their crucial first days of life
