AB  - BIRDS Abstract: Licenses to hunt endangered Long-tailed Ducks in southern Finland have been repealed after BirdLife International took authorities to court. Long-tailed Duck is classified worldwide as endangered, but in southern Finland, a license for spring hunting of the species was authorised in 2011, further threatening the survival of the population. BirdLife Finland and its local member organisation are working to save the species, and lodged a complaint to the Supreme Administrative Court of Finland. This proved successful as the court found the license for spring hunting illegal
