TI  - Eland bull dominance; De Beers help SANParke Namakwa Nasionale Park uitbrei; Wilddiewe, pasop!; Strategy on lion conservation on cards
AU  - Anon
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - Briefly discusses some issues regarding the wildlife industry, such as a report of scientists from London and Copenhagen on the clicking sounds made by walking eland bulls that correlate to body size and were signals to show their fighting potential, thus establishing mating rights. Refers to De Beers Consolidated Mines cooperating with South African National Parks (SANParks) to include 36 thousand hectare of West Coast farms in the planned transfrontier conservation area of the Namaqua National Park. States it will be the fifth largest national park in South Africa and important to ensure the only arid biodiversity hotspot in the world since the key components of the Succulent Karoo Biome. Briefly mentions illegal hunting practices in California, USA that caused heavy fines to hunters. Warns that game poachers and illegal hunters of Africa could also receive heavy penalties to give a better image to safari hunting. Includes an insert on experts meeting in Windhoek, Namibia to map out a strategy on lion conservation, following a debate to restrict trade in trophies at the CITES Conference of Parties 13, held in Bangkok four years ago. Emphasises the need for this conservation because of the decrease in lion population in some African countries
