TI  - Malta and Italy still don't get it
AU  - Anon, A
T2  - Birdwatch Magazine
AB  - BIRDS Abstract: BirdLife Malta and LIPU-BirdLife Italy keep the transparently illegal hunting of birds on the European-African migratory highway under observation every year, and have reported that the problem is still widespread, despite an 11 per cent decline from last year. The EU Birds Directive expressly and strictly forbids the hunting of wild birds in spring to allow their numbers to replenish, but raptors and other protected species are illegal to shoot year-round
