AB  - The article reports on the decreasing number of red-shanked douc langurs based on a survey in the Son Tra Nature Reserve in Vietnam. It mentions that groups of the specie is becoming endangered. According to the author, the group of red-shanked douc langur is composed of 6-24 members in different sizes. In addition, the finding of the survey proves that the Reserve of Vietnem is starting to lose langurs. Causes of the incident such as illegal hunting, frequent trapping and unstructured tourism are also presented.
