TI  - Push to Save Top Predators.
T2  - Wildlife Conservation
AB  - The article focuses on the move of the U.S. Wildlife Conservation Society and its partners to support the Great Cats and Rare Canids Act of 2004. The said bill would provide measures to save snow leopards, lions, wild dogs and then other predators endangered by habitat loss, illegal hunting and human-wildlife conflict. Currently, 83 members of the Congress and 5 Senators have co-sponsored the bill. John Calvelli, senior vice president of WCS, states that every e-mail received by the organization through its Take Action program is a one step closer for the authorization of the bill.
