TY  - JOUR
TI  - Endangered Wildlife Trust update: Help required for Oribi conservation in South Africa
AU  - Evans, S.W.
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - Mentions that the Endangered Wildlife Trust (EWT) is a non-profit conservation organisation focussing on the sustainable management and conservation of natural resources. States the Oribi Working Group is one of the seventeen specialist thematic EWT working groups, aiming to ensure the long-term survival of the oribi (Ourebia ourebi) in their natural grassland habitat. Warns of the sharp decline in oribi numbers, the South African Red Data Book for Mammals classified them as `endangered'. Explains this rapid decline is due to factors such as habitat destruction, as grasslands are lost to forestry, farming, overstocking, erosion and mining. Emphasises over-utilisation due to illegal hunting with dogs and trapping also led to demise of oribi in KwaZulu-Natal. Regrets that inappropriate management namely fencing and poor veld management do not support the co-existence of oribi. Mentions data on oribi localities are maintained in a GIS database and contributes to environmental impact assessments. Points out the Oribi Working Group aims to improve the oribi's conservation status, including objecting to inappropriate developments in oribi grassland habitat, proposing alternatives and translocating oribi to areas where they are better conserved. Provides contact details of the EWT
