TY  - JOUR
TI  - To the Rescue.
AU  - Blake, Stephen
T2  - Wildlife Conservation
AB  - The article focuses on the efforts of wildlife conservationists to protect elephants caught in a wire snare in Gabon. Conservationists were alarmed from the reports of Shell Oil Co. employees in the Gamba Complex of Protected Areas that a large bull forest elephant had been sent with a cable snare. The World Conservation Society and Smithsonian Institution have helped to remove the wire snare from the elephant before it becomes dangerous or die from infection. The author discussed the strategies made by the conservationists in taking off the cable snare in the elephant's leg. The author stresses the need for the conservation community and partners in the private sector to improve efforts to protect elephants from illegal hunting and to promote a conservation ethic for the endangered species.
