TY  - JOUR
TI  - Wie jag so onwettig met die karre?
AU  - Verdoorn, G.H.
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - Addresses the problem of vehicles killing wild animals and birds on South African roads. Regrets that every day and night some illegal hunting occurs when motorists race at top speed without sympathy or empathy for other creatures. Mentions these road kills include small mammals such as rabbits, meercats, smaller cat species, ground squirrels, bat-eared jackal and mongoose. States antelopes, a great many tortoises and owls are also slaughtered. Warns that any unnecessary killing could bring the extinction of some species nearer. Gives examples of ways to prevent this killing, namely keeping within speed limits and being aware of animals or birds next to or on roads. Advises to sound the horn, slacken speed and dimming the lights at night and even stopping to remove tortoises from the road. Provides contact details of Mazda Wildlife Fund Bird Information to report any road kills
