TY  - JOUR
TI  - Far and away
AU  - Michler, I.
T2  - Africa Geographic
AB  - Points out there are few areas left on the African continent that truly qualify as remote, wilderness areas. States although experiences of the true sense of isolation in remote places are becoming less accessible, they can still be found in Mozambique's Niassa National Reserve. Points out it is situated in the far north on the border with Tanzania and the largest yet least visited protected area. Mentions the Niassa covers forty-two thousand square kilometres, in Eastern Miombo Eco-Region, to be included in a planned transfrontier conservation area. Comments on the author's first visit to Niassa in 1997 and a recent return visit. Looks at the rugged beauty of unique landscapes and immense sense of space, with numerous river systems. Focuses on the largest populations of almost all mammal species found in Mozambique that are included in this reserve, with many bird species and a large plant diversity. Warns about the concern for Niassa as it has little protection, its biodiversity neglected for more than 30 years. States although the government has an agreement with Fauna & Flora International, Niassa needs policing as it faces many threats such as illegal harvesting and hunting. Stresses the importance of a low-impact ecotourism industry for stabilisation
