TI  - Rhino Poaching Hotline!
AU  - Coetzee, F.
AU  - Friedmann, Y.
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - Points out that as the Endangered Wildlife Trust (EWT) recognised the dire need to urgently address the escalating problem of rhino poaching, an anti-poaching project was developed. Explains the Rhino Security Project aims to strengthen the security of rhinoceroses on privately owned game farms, as well as formally protected areas. Emphasises that this includes improving communication between rhino owners and relevant government officials and supporting investigations into rhino poaching incidences. States that often members of the public become aware of information about poaching incidents or sale of rhino horns, which should be reported to the authorities. Warns that it is a criminal offense to not report a wildlife crime, therefore the EWT launched the Rhino Poaching Hotline in order that such information can be submitted for appropriate investigative action by enforcement agencies. Stresses the importance of South African citizens becoming involved in the fight against the wanton killing of our rhino, since already 153 rhinos have been poached between January and the end of July 2010. Mentions also that landowners should report individuals offering to dehorn their rhino and then trying to buy these horns. Provides contact details of EWT
