TY  - JOUR
TI  - PHASA on lion debate; Stern warning by Namibian PH's; Wettige vuurwapens `nie oorsaak van hoe misdaad'
AU  - Anon
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - Briefly discusses lion hunting in South Africa. States the Professional Hunters' Association of South Africa (PHASA) has reconsidered its position, thereby supporting the hunting of any species that have been released into an extensive wildlife system, hunted according to the laws of the land and the commonly accepted principles of fair chase. Points out that therefore unethical and illegal practices will not be tolerated, as our country's and the hunters' reputations would be damaged. Refers also to the warning of the Namibia Professional Hunting Association (Napha) in terms of any misconduct by their members or non-members that could jeopardise the future of their hunting sector. Explains thus the issuing of leopard and cheetah trophy hunting permits in Namibia have been suspended for 2010. Includes a discussion on the Confederation of Hunting Associations of South Africa (CHASA) alarm about the recent statements made by President Zuma and the Minister of Police with regard to the number of legal firearms contributing to the high level of crime. Emphasises CHASA felt these remarks are untruthful and were caused by officials misguiding them regarding crime statistics in terms of firearms, thus CHASA wants to discuss the issue with President Zuma
