TY  - JOUR
TI  - Strengthening Environmental Governance Framework
AU  - Anon
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - Points out that the Law and Policy Working Group of the Endangered Wildlife Trust (EWT) recently launched a new project fully funded by the Howard G. Buffet Foundation's African Cheetah Intiative, namely `Strengthening South Africa's Environmental Governance Framework'. Emphasises that efficient biodiversity management and conservation can only be achieved if supported by sound implementation, monitoring, compliance and enforcement. States this project aims to promote good governance and providing targeted training for stakeholders, contributing to the existing environmental governance framework. Comments on this project implemented in all nine provinces, with the focus on biodiversity issues, including non-compliance with environmental law, pollution and illegal development activities. Explains that the EWT working groups had encountered situations where animals were killed by illegal shooting such as honey badger, leopard and cheetah currently afforded protection under the Threatened and Protected Species Regulations. Relates the poisoning of a waterhole to kill rhinos for their horns, but which also killed many other wild animals. Appeals to all South African to report incidents of non-compliance with legislation. Provides contact details
