TY  - JOUR
TI  - Is dit norm(e)aal en standaard?
AU  - Verdoorn, G.H.
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - Looks at the new proposed National Norms and Standards on the Regulation of the Hunting Industry in South Africa. Askes why hunters were not informed of a new set of rules but had to hear it through the media, especially since they had themselves proposed more severe norms and standards. Points out that although the document has positive merits, the issues concerning professional and ordinary hunters had been confused. Comments on hunting ethics that are not directly addressed in the document, however every hunter should ascertain what the document proposes. States dedicated bakkie hunters would in future have to walk and stalk their prey since no more hunting from vehicles are allowed. Warns of illegal use of bait, snares, trapping, poison and hunting dogs. Discusses the rifles and handguns developed for hunting that are allowed, excluding poach ketties and airguns. Emphasises to upheld the norms and standards and to ensure the maintaining of fair hunting principles with appreciation towards the wild animals of the veld
