AU  - Sowry, T.
AU  - Anon
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - Briefly discusses activities regarding the wildlife industry, such as the 7th graduation ceremony of the Southern African Wildlife College held in October 2004, with 44 students graduating, some from other SADC countries. Refers to a game rancher's study tour of the Northern Game Organisation, planned to visit New Zeeland in April 2005. States that the former Minister of Environmental Affairs and Tourism, Valli Moosa was elected as President of the World Conservation Union (IUCN) for next four years during its 3rd Congress in November 2004. Comments on the conviction of G. Pretorius of Nonile hunting concession for fraud, theft and contavening the KwaZulu-Natal Nature Conservation Ordinance, allowing a German client to shoot a rhino which did not belong to Pretorius. Invites the public to participate in the first national Giant Bullfrog Survey of the Endangered Wildlife Trust and the University of Pretoria. Explains this survey aimed at acquiring distribution data of the giant bullfrog (Pyxicephalus adspersus) to develop effective conservation measures in key habitats. Urges the participants to photograph bullfrogs they encounter, submitting this with one entry form per locality to stand a chance of winning prizes
