TI  - Was the RSPCA right to spend £330k on hunt case?
T2  - Daily Mail
AB  - THE sheer arrogance of the convicted animal abusers of David Cameron's hunt, the Heythrop, beggars belief. The court was shown evidence of illegal hunting on several occasions but former hunt master Julian Barnfield stated he 'only pleaded guilty as he couldn't afford to fight the case'. What drivel. This hunt continues to hunt despite the law, as do many others. As for Barnfield also suggesting people should stop funding the RSPCA as it used large amounts of donated money to pursue this conviction, this is just what the RSPCA should be doing, pursuing those who are arrogantly being cruel to animals and believe they are above the law. [ABSTRACT FROM PUBLISHER]
