AB  - Reports that in mid-1983 the Namibia Wildlife Trust started what came to be known as the auxiliary game guard system. Apart from finding evidence of illegal hunting the game guards have undoubtedly played a major role in deterring would-be poachers. For the first time in fifteen years the number of big game had increased in the region. Illustrates with photographs
