TI  - Renosterkritiek teen Kruger `ongevraag'; Vuurwapenregistrasie- inbelsentrum help dalk; EWT joins forces with Wild Cheetah Project; Mens moet nou se van dooie renoster; Help the EWT count oribi
AU  - Anon
AU  - Rossouw, A.
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - Briefly mentions the negative reaction of the media and animal rights groups when 10 out of 300 white rhinos died during translocation to private land. States the South African Hunters and Game Conservation Association explained that limited animal mortality is unfortunately a factor in translocation, however it is an important conservation principle to distribute genetic material. Refers to a call centre of the SAPS to communicate with firearm owners with regard to the renewal of their licences. Mentions carnivore conservation strengthened by the EWT (Endangered Wildlife Trust) Wildlife Conflict Prevention Group joining forces with the Wild Cheetah Project. Explains that conflicts between farmers and communities and predators will be resolved. Comments on CHASA supporting laws against illegal hunting and trade in rhino horn, in connection with the National Biodiversity Act published in July 2009 in the Government Gazette. Looks at the national bi-annual oribi census of the EWT Oribi Working Group. Points out that help is needed to count oribi in order to allow conservationists to determine trends in their population, guiding future conservation management decisions and determining the current primary threats. Provides contact details
