TY  - JOUR
TI  - Advanced field guiding. Part 35: Poaching. Part 1
AU  - Cheney, C.
T2  - Wild & jag = Game & hunt
AB  - States as the general public is aware of poaching issues because of the amount of sensational media exposure, questions relating to poaching activities are therefore frequently posed to a field guide. Emphasises it is necessary to differentiate between two types of poachers, namely subsistence poachers and commercial poachers. Explains the one is driven by the need to survive such as the unemployed poor with a starving family and the other driven by greed, namely commercial poaching crime syndicates orchestrated by wealthy individuals. Mentions these commercial poaching operations are often highly organised and well equipped, killing more animals than necessary, or targeting creatures whose body parts are in demand. Deplores the type of poaching where rangers and field staff entrusted to protect wildlife, abuse their positions and become directly involved with poaching for personal gain. Looks at anti-poaching operations, sometimes taking on the scale of a small war with both sides equipped as small military units
DA  - 2006/01/01/
PY  - 2006
DP  - EBSCOhost
VL  - 12
IS  - 7
SP  - 20
