TI  - Highlights: Crime and Punishment in PRC 17 Jan - 04 Feb 2007
DA  - 2007/01/01/
PY  - 2007
DP  - EBSCOhost
UR  - https://search.ebscohost.com/login.aspx?direct=true&db=awn&AN=20070206478001&site=ehost-live
DB  - awn
N1  - <p>Note: Highlights: Crime and Punishment in PRC 17 Jan - 04 Feb 2007&nbsp;&nbsp; The following is a compilation of reports on crimes, sentences, punishments, and other judicial related activities in the PRC monitored from 17 January to 4 February 2007. The sources are indicated in brackets after each report.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; NOTE: THE FOLLOWING CONTENTS MAY CONTAIN ACTIVE EXTERNAL HTML LINKS&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Anti-Narcotics Operations&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Beijing&nbsp;&nbsp; Beijing Customs Units Achieve Results Against Drug-Smuggling Crimes in 2006 -- According to the 31 January issue of Beijing Ribao, in 2006, Beijing Customs Units solved 12 drug smuggling cases, confiscating 17 kilograms [kg] of narcotics. In January 2007, they solved five drug smuggling cases, confiscating 8 kg of narcotics.[Beijing Beijing Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Beijing Municipal CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Guangdong&nbsp;&nbsp; Baiyun Airport Customs Office Solves Drug Smuggling Cases -- According to the 24 January issue of Guangzhou Ribao, Baiyun Airport Customs Officials examined cargo on an Ethiopia flight from Addis Ababa, discovering 27.8 kg of marijuana leaves hidden inside 215 pairs of platform shoes. Since 4 September 2006, Guangzhou Customs has solved 85 drug smuggling cases, confiscating 144 kg of narcotics. [Guangzhou Guangzhou Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Guangzhou City CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp; According to the 30 January issue of Guangzhou Ribao, on 29 January 2007, Baiyun Airport Safety Inspection Personnel examined a drawbar traveling bag of a young female Indonesian passenger, discovering over 1.7 kg of "ice" in the double layer of the bag. [Guangzhou Guangzhou Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Guangzhou City Intermediate Court Tries Drug Making and Trafficking Case -- According to the 24 January issue of Guangzhou Ribao, the court tried six criminal gangsters, including He Lirong (0149 4409 2837), Huang Wuwei (7806 2477 3956), and Huang Yanping (7806 3508 1627) for drug making and trafficking. From late 2003 to 2005, He instructed Huang Wuwei and Huang Yanping to transport drug-making materials from Guangzhou to a pig farm in Taishan to produce "ecstasy" pills in powder form. They processed the powder into "ecstasy" pills in a Taishan chemical plant. He hired others to produce "ecstasy" pills in a Taishan pastry processing plant and transported the drugs to Guangzhou for sale. Police searched residences of these criminal suspects, confiscating 740 kg of "ecstasy" pills and powder. [Guangzhou Guangzhou Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Shantou Customs Personnel Confiscate Three Kg of Heroin -- According to 3 February issue of Guangzhou Ribao, on 19 January 2007, Shantou Airport Customs Personnel examined a traveling bag of a young Malaysian woman passenger from a Thai flight, discovering three kg of heroin number 3. The woman claimed that she was forced by someone to carry the drugs into China. [Guangzhou Guangzhou Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Guangxi&nbsp;&nbsp; Guangxi and Vietnam Police Jointly Smash "Golden Triangle Region" Drug Trafficking Passage -- According to a 26 January dispatch from Zhongguo Xinwen Wang, in 2006, Guangxi Police solved over 6,000 drug criminal cases, confiscating 80 kg of heroin. Since 1996, Guangxi Police had confiscated over 2,400 kg of heroin, more than 80 percent of which was smuggled from the "Golden Triangle" Region via Vietnam into China. In 2006, Guangxi Police strengthened its cooperation with Vietnamese counterparts to smash the drug smuggling passage. They also strengthened cooperation with Vietnamese counterparts, solving over 40 cross-border women and children trafficking cases, smashing 8 gangs, rescuing 171 abducted Vietnamese women. [Guangzhou Dayang Wang (Internet Version-WWW) in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; http://china.dayoo.com/gb/content/2007-01/26/content_2744883.htm&nbsp;&nbsp; Guizhou&nbsp;&nbsp; Guiyang City Police Solve Drug Trafficking Case -- According to the 20 January issue of Guizhou Ribao, on 13 January 2007, based on reports from the masses, Guiyang Police arrested a drug trafficker and his girlfriend, confiscating 10 grams [g] of heroin and five "ecstasy" pills. On 14 January 2007, police captured three drug traffickers, confiscating 775 g of "K" powder. The drug traffickers admitted they obtained the drugs from An Mao (1344 5399), a Sichuan drug supplier. With the collaboration of Sichuan Police, a Guiyang police task group captured three gangsters, headed by Wang Yi (3769 5030), confiscating 3 kg-plus of "K" powder. [Guiyang Guizhou Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Guizhou Provincial CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Guiyang Railway Police Solve Drug Transportation Case -- According to the 26 January issue of Renmin Gongan Bao, on 21 January 2007, Guiyang Railway Police solved a drug transport case, arresting two sisters in the Liupanshui railway station, confiscating 2.1 kg of heroin. The sisters claimed that a Guizhou Bijie native asked them to transport the drugs to Guiyang. [Beijing Renmin Gongan Bao in Chinese -- newspaper reporting primarily on public security issues, sponsored by the Ministry of Public Security - MPS]&nbsp;&nbsp; Hainan&nbsp;&nbsp; Haikou City Police Solve 843 Drug Criminal Cases in 2006 -- According to the 22 January issue of Renmin Gongan Bao, in 2006, Haikou Police solved 843 drug criminal cases, confiscating 8.3 kg of narcotics. They smashed 12 trans-regional drug trafficking gangs, arresting a number of foreign drug lords. They smashed the "Burma-Yunnan-Hainan," "Vietnam-Guangxi-Hainan," and "Guangdong-Hainan" drug trafficking passages. They sent 2,744 drug addicts to drug detoxification centers for treatment, and 759 repeated addicts to education through labor. They searched 33 drug-related entertainment places, capturing 260 persons for using "ecstasy" pills and "K" powder. [Beijing Renmin Gongan Bao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Heilongjiang&nbsp;&nbsp; Heilongjiang Police Confiscate 88.9 Kg of Marijuana -- According to the 20 January issue of Xinhua Meiri Dianxun, Jiamusi Police joined with Xinjiang Police to solve an extraordinary marijuana making and trafficking case, capturing nine criminal suspects, confiscating 88.93 kg of marijuana. [Beijing Xinhua Meiri Dianxun in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Hunan&nbsp;&nbsp; Daoxian County Police Smash Drug Trafficking Gang -- According to the 22 January issue of Renmin Gongan Bao, Yongzhou Daoxian County Public Security Bureau [PSB] smashed a drug trafficking gang, capturing 14 criminal suspects, confiscating over 1.9 kg of heroin, freezing 200,000 yuan of drug money.[Beijing Renmin Gongan Bao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Jiangxi&nbsp;&nbsp; Jiangxi Province Solves 1,052 Drug Cases in 2006 -- According to the 27 January issue of Renmin Gongan Bao, in 2006, Police Province-Wide solved 1,052 drug cases, capturing 2,111 persons, confiscating 12.45 kg of heroin, 8,030 "ecstasy" pills, 6.42 kg of "K" powder, and 38,044 methamphetamine tablets. They sent 1,752 addicts to drug detoxification centers for treatment and 522 repeated addicts to education through labor. [Beijing Renmin Gongan Bao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Liaoning&nbsp;&nbsp; Dalian Customs Office Solves "Ice" Smuggling Case -- According to the 30 January issue of Renmin Gongan Bao, in its initial trial, Dalian City Intermediate People's Court sentenced three drug smugglers, including a Japanese, to death. In July 2003, Dalian Customs Anti-Smuggling Bureau solved three "ice" smuggling cases, confiscating 3.77 kg of "ice," capturing three criminal suspects including a Japanese and a Korean. On 18 June 2004, a police task group formed by Dalian Customs Office and Liaoning Public Security Department [PSD], arrested three criminal suspects in Shenzhen, confiscating 3.1 kg of "ice." [Beijing Renmin Gongan Bao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ningxia&nbsp;&nbsp; Ningxia Public Security Narcotics Control Units Solve 4,086 Drug-Related Cases in 2006 -- According to the 30 January issue of Renmin Gongan Bao, in 2006, Ningxia Police solved 4,086 drug criminal cases, capturing 4,331 persons, confiscating 15.22 kg of heroin, 1.36 kg of "K" powder, and 245 kg of marijuana products. They sent 2,973 addicts to drug detoxification centers for treatment and 896 repeated addicts to education through labor. [Beijing Renmin Gongan Bao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Zhejiang&nbsp;&nbsp; Wenzhou City PSB Solves Drug Trafficking Case -- According to the 23 January issue of Zhejiang Ribao, on 17 January 2007, a Wenzhou narcotics control police unit captured criminal suspects Zhang Shuhai (1728 3219 3189) and Zhang Ling (1728 7325), confiscating 8.17 kg of narcotics. In November 2006, a police unit learned that a drug trafficker surnamed Jiang trafficked in drugs in Wenzhou City. On 16 January 2007, a police task group learned that Jiang obtained the narcotics in Shenzhen. On 17 January 2007, civilian policemen arrested Zhang Shuhai and Zhang Ling in Wenzhou, confiscating 3 kg of "K" powder and 2 kg of "ice." They searched the residences of the criminal suspects, confiscating 30,000 methamphetamine tablets, 270 g of "ice," and 400 "ecstasy" pills. They arrested Jin, another criminal suspect, confiscating 800 methamphetamine tablets and 50 g of "ice." [Hangzhou Zhejiang Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Zhejiang Provincial CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Anti-Smuggling Operations&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; National&nbsp;&nbsp; Chinese Customs Units Solve 7,240 Smuggling Cases in 2006 -- According to the 26 January issue of Fazhi Ribao, in 2006, Chinese Customs Units solved 7,240 smuggling cases worth 13.7 billion yuan, an increase of 30 percent over 2005. Guangzhou and Nanning Customs Units jointly solved a smuggling case involving 2,043 cars worth 600 million yuan.&nbsp;&nbsp;Gongbei Customs Unit solved an electronic and video game smuggling case, worth 118 million yuan, capturing 42 gangsters. Qingdao Customs Unit solved automobile air-conditioning part smuggling cases, worth 280 million yuan. Chinese Customs Units solved 152 processing trade smuggling cases, worth 1.22 billion yuan. They solved 242 price-concealing cases worth 3.27 billion yuan. [Beijing Fazhi Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Ministry of Justice covering China's legal units]&nbsp;&nbsp; Guangdong&nbsp;&nbsp; Shenzhen City Intermediate People's Court Tries Cigarette Smuggling Case -- According to the 23 January issue of Guangzhou Ribao, the court tried 20 criminal suspects from Shishi, Fujian, and Huilai, in Guangdong Province, for involvement in a general goods smuggling case.&nbsp;&nbsp; In early 2004, Lu and Lin purchased fishing boats and speedboats to smuggle cigarettes into China in the Shishi sea area. Lin purchased cigarettes in Hong Kong and shipped them to the Philippines. Lu smuggled these cigarettes from the Shishi sea area into China. These gangsters evaded 1.2 billion yuan in taxes. [Guangzhou Guangzhou Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Zhuhai Gongbei Customs Office Solves 3,000 Smuggling Cases in 2006 -- According to the 24 January issue of Guangzhou Ribao, in 2006, Gongbei Customs Office solved 2,984 smuggling cases, worth 2.57 billion yuan, evading 150 million yuan in taxes. The customs office solved nine disassembled automobile smuggling cases. [Guangzhou Guangzhou Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Guangxi&nbsp;&nbsp; Nanning Customs Units Solve 868 Smuggling Cases in 2006 -- According to the 23 January issue of Fazhi Kuai Bao, in 2006, Nanning Customs Anti-Smuggling Units solved 868 smuggling cases worth 208 million yuan, evading 18.5 million yuan in taxes. They arrested 145 criminal suspects. [Nanning Fazhi Kuai Bao in Chinese -- newspaper reporting primarily on political and legal issues sponsored by the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region Politics and Law Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Campaign Against Firearms and Explosives&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Guangxi&nbsp;&nbsp; Laibin City Police Smash Illegal Gun-Making Den -- According to the 19 January issue of Fazhi Kuai Bao, on 18 January 2007, Laibin City Police smashed an illegal gun-making den. On 25 December 2006, a police task group arrested Wei Wenying (7279 2429 5391) at his residence, confiscated gun-making tools and 16 homemade sand-grit guns. [Nanning Fazhi Kuai Bao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Shanghai&nbsp;&nbsp; Shanghai Municipal Police Solve Gun-Trafficking Case -- According to the 26 January issue of Dongfang Zaobao, Shanghai Railway PSB solved a gun-trafficking case, capturing 32 criminal suspects, confiscating 25 guns, three vehicles, and 22 cellular phones, smashing a "Southwestern China to Anhui, Zhejiang Province" gun-trafficking passage. On 8 November 2006, railway police arrested two criminal suspects on a Chengdu-Hefei train, confiscating four pistols. On 11 November 2006, a police task group arrested 11 criminal suspects during a gun transaction in Huainan. They arrested more criminal suspects in Anhui, Zhejiang, Sichuan, and Shanghai. [Guangzhou Dayang Wang (Internet Version-WWW) in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; http://china.dayoo.com/gb/content/2007-01/26/content_2744905.htm&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Economic Crimes&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Anhui&nbsp;&nbsp; Chaohu City Intermediate People's Court Tries Issuance of False Value Added Specialized Tax Invoice Case -- According to the 21 January issue of Anhui Ribao, on 19 January 2007, in its initial trial, the court sentenced Gao Guowei (7559 0948 0251) to death with a reprieve of two years for issuance of false value added specialized tax invoices for over 400 companies in 11 provinces with face value of over 200 million yuan. Gao used his four companies to issue 486 false invoices for other units, evading 6.57 million yuan in taxes. He obtained 359 false invoices from other units, evading 6.16 million yuan in taxes. He produced 10,624 false railway transportation invoices for his own companies, evading 8.46 million yuan in taxes. He also issued 2,472 false railway transportation invoices for other units, evading 1.99 million yuan in taxes. Gao also coerced others to issue eight false value added specialized tax invoices, evading 122,699 yuan in taxes. [Hefei Anhui Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Anhui Provincial CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp; Shanghai&nbsp;&nbsp; Minhang District Court Punishes Former Company Chairman for Taking Public Deposits Illegally -- According to the 24 January issue of Jiefang Ribao, the court sentenced Gao Jianzhong (7559 1696 0022), former Chairman of Jiabi Company, a Chinese-foreign equity joint venture, to 10 years imprisonment for illegally taking public deposits. From 1996 to June 2003, Gao signed contracts with 1,588 clients, offering high interest rates, accepting 19.14 million yuan of public deposits. [Shanghai Jiefang Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Shanghai Municipal CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp; Shanghai Municipal PSB Smashes Swindling Gang -- According to the 22 January issue of Jiefang Ribao, Shanghai PSB smashed a swindling gang, arresting eight criminal suspects. A Shanghai Court sentenced Xie Changhua (6200 7022 5478), a principal female criminal suspect, to life imprisonment for obtaining public deposits illegally and swindling crimes. On 8 April 2005, a number of Shanghai residents reported to police that they had purchased fake United States [US] Nasdaq Composite stock shares from the swindlers. On 13 April 2005, police captured Xie and seven other gangsters. Xie, in collusion with her husband and other gangsters, printed fake US stock shares including Broadway International Development Company and American Shanghai Chemical Industry Company, producing false public listing information to swindle 40 million yuan from over 670 persons. [Shanghai Jiefang Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Illegal Immigration and Emigration&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; National&nbsp;&nbsp; Public Security Border Defense Units Nationwide Solve 1,143 Illegal Migration and 1,700 Smuggling Cases in 2006 -- According to the 24 January issue of Fazhi Ribao, in 2006, Border Defense Police units nationwide solved 1,143 illegal migration cases, involving 2,422 persons and 475 illegal migration organizers and "snakeheads"; plus 1,700 smuggling case worth 230 million yuan. They solved 4,458 drug trafficking cases, arresting 4,777 criminal suspects, confiscating 3,999 kg of narcotics; and 206 gun-related cases, confiscating 1,167 guns. They solved 9,346 criminal cases and 30,687 public order cases, capturing 694 Ministry of Public Security [MPS] Internet-wanted fugitives. [Beijing Fazhi Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Jilin&nbsp;&nbsp; Jilin Public Security Border Defense General Corps Solves 246 Illegal Migration Cases in 2006 -- According to the 20 January issue of Renmin Gongan Bao, in 2006, Jilin Border Defense General Corps solved 246 illegal migration cases, capturing 810 stowaways, and 80 organizers and "snakeheads." [Beijing Renmin Gongan Bao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Shandong&nbsp;&nbsp; Shandong Border Defense General Corps Solves 243 Illegal Migration Cases in 2006 -- According to the 27 January issue of Dazhong Ribao, in 2006, Border Defense Units province-wide solved 243 illegal migration cases, capturing 444 persons. They solved the "1 October 2006" Yantai, "22 April 2006" Weihai, and "9 June 2006" Qingdao migration cases. [Jinan Dazhong Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Shandong Provincial CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp; Weihai Border Defense Police Solve Illegal Migration Cases -- According to the 20 January of Dazhong Ribao, from 14 to 16 January 2007, Weihai Border Defense Police solved several illegal migration cases, capturing over 40 stowaways. On 14 January 2007, a Weihai Border Defense Police Unit solved an illegal migration case, capturing 13 gangsters headed by Huang. Since 2006, Huang, in collusion with others, had produced false identity and business trip documents, helping others to obtain business visas, smuggling themselves to the Republic of Korea [ROK]. On 15 January 2007, a Weihai Border Defense Police Unit smashed a gang headed by Zhu. On 16 January 2007, they arrested an "organizer" and 16 stowaways. [Jinan Dazhong Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Official Corruption, Embezzlement&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; National&nbsp;&nbsp; Chinese Discipline Inspection and Supervision Units Investigate 20,768 Rural Grassroots-Level Cadre in 2006 for Discipline and Regulation Violations -- According to a 2 February dispatch from Xinhua Wang, in 2006, discipline and supervision units nationwide investigated 20,768 rural grassroots-level cadre, penalizing 20,283 persons. They aimed at improving Party work style and construction of clean and honest administration at rural grassroots-level. [Guangzhou Dayang Wang (Internet-WWW) in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; http://china.dayoo.com/gb/content/2007-02/02/content_2752184.htm&nbsp;&nbsp; Anhui&nbsp;&nbsp; Former Provincial Financial Department Director Tried for Bribe-Taking -- According to the 17 January issue of Anhui Ribao, in its final trial, the Provincial Higher People's Court upheld the original verdict, sentenced Kuang Bingwen (0562 3521 2429), former Director of the Provincial Financial Department, to 15 years imprisonment for bribe-taking. The court sentenced Kuang Zhongping (0562 0022 1627), son of Kuang Bingwen, a staff member of the Provincial Trust Investment Company, to five years imprisonment. From early 1993 to 1998, Kuang Bingwen helped other units to obtain loans, fund allocations, and individuals to get promoted. He accepted 961,000 yuan and USD 51,000 in bribes. In collusion with his son, Kuang, he accepted 320,000 yuan in bribes. [Hefei Anhui Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Former Provincial Public Health Department Deputy Director Tried for Bribe-Taking -- According to a 3 February dispatch from Xinhua Domestic Service, on 2 February 2007, in its initial trial, Anqing City Intermediate People's Court sentenced Shang Jun (1424 6511), former Deputy Director of the Provincial Public Health Department, to 10 years imprisonment for bribe-taking and possession of a huge amount of unaccounted for assets. From 1992 to 2005, during his tenures in Fuyang Prefecture and Fuyang City, Shang abused his power, helped others to get promoted and to obtain construction projects, accepting 900,000 yuan and USD 200 in bribes. He also possessed 980,000 in unaccounted for yuan unaccounted for. [Guangzhou Dayang Wang (Internet-WWW) in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; http://china.dayoo.com/gb/content/2007-02/03/content_2752611.htm&nbsp;&nbsp; Former Chaohu City Government Deputy Secretary-General Tried for Bribe-Taking -- According to a 4 February dispatch from Xinhua Wang, on 2 February 2007, Chaohu City Intermediate People's Court sentenced Ling Jianguo (0407 1696 0948), former Deputy Secretary-General of Chaohu City Government, to six years imprisonment for bribe-taking. During his tenures as Deputy Magistrate of Hanshan County and Deputy Secretary of the County Party Committee, Ling sought benefits for others, accepting 250,000 yuan in bribes. [Guangzhou Dayang Wang (Internet-WWW) in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; http://china.dayoo.com/gb/content/2007-02/04/content_2752940.htm&nbsp;&nbsp; Former Fuyang City Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference [CPPCC] Vice-Chairman Tried for Bribe-Taking -- According to the 30 January issue of Anhui Shichang Bao, on 29 January 2007, in its initial trial, Chuzhou City Intermediate Court sentenced Liu Jiayi (0491 1367 5030), age 61, former Vice-Chairman of Fuyang City CPPCC, to 13 years imprisonment for bribe-taking. From November 1989 to April 2004, during his tenures as Secretary of Lixin County Committee and President of Fuyang City Intermediate People's Court, Liu abused his power, sought benefits for others in engineering construction projects and personnel promotion, accepted 901,500 yuan, 10,000 yuan of gift cards, 90 silver coins, one notebook computer, two air conditioners, and one furniture set in bribes from 23 persons.[Guangzhou Dayang Wang (Internet Version-WWW) in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; http://china.dayoo.com/gb/content/2007-01/30/content_2747940.htm&nbsp;&nbsp; Former Fuyang City Intermediate People's Court President Tried for Bribe-Taking -- According to a 30 January dispatch from Xinhua Wang,&nbsp;&nbsp;Lu'an City Intermediate People's Court sentenced Zhang Zimin (1728 5261 3046), former President of Fuyang City Intermediate People's Court, to 9 years imprisonment for bribe-taking and possession of a huge amount of unaccounted for assets. Since 2004, Zhang sought benefits for others in project bids and personnel promotions, accepting over 800,000 yuan in bribes and possessing 580,000 yuan worth of unaccounted for assets. [Guangzhou Dayang Wang (Internet Version-WWW) in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; http://china.dayoo.com/gb/content/2007-01/30/content_2748957.htm&nbsp;&nbsp; Fujian&nbsp;&nbsp; Former Sanming Tobacco Monopoly Bureau Director Sentenced to Death for Graft, Public Fund Embezzlement, and Power Abuse -- According to the 26 January issue of Fazhi Ribao, in its final trial, Fujian Provincial Higher People's Court upheld the original verdict, sentenced Xu Ximing (6079 6932 2494), former Director of Sanming Tobacco Monopoly Bureau, to death for graft, public fund embezzlement, and causing economic losses to the country.&nbsp;&nbsp;During his tenure as Director of the City Tobacco Monopoly Bureau and Manager of the Tobacco Branch Company, Xu obtained 16.79 million yuan illegally, embezzling 10 million yuan of public funds for stock share investment, accepting 3.37 million yuan and HKD 11,000 in bribes. He abused his power, causing 10.46 million yuan of economic losses for the country. [Beijing Fazhi Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Gansu&nbsp;&nbsp; Former Provincial Power Supply Company Financial Division Director Sentenced to Life Imprisonment for Graft, Bribe-Taking, and Public Fund Embezzlement -- According to the 24 January issue of Fazhi Ribao, in its final trial, Gansu Provincial Higher People's Court sentenced Gu Huijuan (7357 1979 1227), female, former Director of the Financial Division of the Provincial Power Supply Company, to 10 years imprisonment for graft, bribe-taking, and public fund embezzlement. On 26 August 2006, in its initial trial, Gansu City Intermediate People's Court sentenced Gu to 13 years imprisonment. Gu accepted 386,000 yuan from other units and embezzling 10.87 million yuan of public funds for stock speculation. She also illegally obtained 12.5 million yuan of public funds. [Beijing Fazhi Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Guangdong&nbsp;&nbsp; Guangzhou Procuratorate Units Investigate 273 Cadre at and above Division Level -- According to the 26 January issue of Guangzhou Ribao, over the past four years, procuratorate units have investigated 1,163 graft and bribery cases involving 1,213 persons, including 242 cadre at county (division) level and 31 cadre at department level. They have investigated 1,330 job-related criminal cases involving 1,380 persons, redeeming 360 million yuan in direct economic losses. [Guangzhou Guangzhou Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Hebei&nbsp;&nbsp; Hebei Provincial Procuratorate Work Report -- According to the 31 January issue of Hebei Ribao, on 18 January 2007, during the 5th Plenary Session of the 10th Provincial People's Congress, Wang Qijiang (3769 0366 3068), Chief Procurator of Hebei Provincial People's Procuratorate, reported that, in 2006, procuratorate units approved the arrests of 36,143 criminal suspects, initiating prosecution of 40,174 persons. They also approved the arrests of 634 criminal syndicate-like organization and hooligan gangsters. They investigated 1,529 government officials including 62 cadre at and above county (division) level, redeeming 234 million yuan in economic losses. From August 2005 to December 2006, they solved 668 commercial bribery cases, involving 23.87 million yuan. These involved 27 cadre at county (division) level and two cadre at department (bureau) level. [Shijiazhuang Hebei Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Jiangsu&nbsp;&nbsp; Jiangsu Province Procuratorate Units Investigate 1,756 Job-Related Criminal Cases in 2006 -- According to the 17 January issue of Xinhua Ribao, in 2006, procuratorate units province-wide investigated 1,756 graft, bribery, and dereliction of duty cases, involving 1,831 persons, including 116 cadre at county (division) level and 10 cadre at department level, redeeming 416 million yuan in direct economic losses. [Nanjing Xinhua Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Jiangsu Provincial CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp; Jiangxi&nbsp;&nbsp; Jiangxi Province Procuratorate Units Investigate 73 Cadre at and above County (Division) Level in 2006 -- According to the 18 January issue of Jiangxi Ribao, in 2006, procuratorate units province-wide solved 1,001 job-related criminal cases involving 1,163 persons, including 70 cadre at county (division) level and 3 cadre at department level. They captured 39 fugitive officials involved in graft and bribery cases. [Nanchang Jiangxi Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Jiangxi Provincial CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp; Liaoning&nbsp;&nbsp; Former Fushun City People's Procuratorate Deputy Procurator Tried for Bribe-Taking -- According to a 31 January dispatch from Xinhua Wang, in its final trial, Shenyang City Intermediate People's Court sentenced Wu Xing'an (0702 5281 1344), former Deputy Procurator of Fushun City People's Procuratorate, age 43, to 13 years imprisonment for bribe-taking. In February 2003, during his tenure as Director of the Anti-Corruption Bureau of Fushun City People's Procuratorate, Wu helped Teng, Director of a credit cooperative in obtaining bail. From 2000 to 2003, Wu helped Zhao, a trader in a coking coal transaction, accepting 700,000 yuan and a watch worth 25,000 yuan. [Guangzhou Dayang Wang (Internet Version - WWW) in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; http://china.dayoo.com/gb/content/2007-01/31/content_2749921.htm&nbsp;&nbsp; Former Fuxin City Party Committee Secretary Punished for Power Abuse -- According to the 30 January issue of Fazhi Ribao, on 29 January 2007, in its initial trial, Dandong City Zhenxing District People's Court sentenced Wang Yachen (3769 0068 1820), former Secretary of Fuxin City Party Committee, to eight years imprisonment for false registered capital reporting and power abuse. Wang and others used false documents to register Hualong Company. [Beijing Fazhi Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ningxia&nbsp;&nbsp; Ningxia Hui Autonomous Region Procuratorate Units Investigate 188 Graft and Bribery Cases in 2006 -- According to the 24 January issue of Ningxia Ribao, in 2006, procuratorate units region wide investigated 188 graft and bribery cases, involving 230 persons, including 3 cadre at department level, redeeming 22.77 million yuan in economic losses. These included: bribe-taking and the possession of a huge amount of unaccounted for asset case of Wang Yingfu (3769 5391 4395), former Inspector of the Regional CPPCC; public fund embezzlement case of Sun Dianhua (1327 3013 5478), former Chairman of Dagu Railway Company; and graft case of Xu Fuxin (1776 4395 2450), former Director of Shijuishan Medical Insurance Center. [Yinchuan Ningxia Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Shaanxi&nbsp;&nbsp; Shaanxi Discipline Inspection and Supervision Units Punish 109 Cadre at and above County (Division) Level for Discipline Violations in 2006 -- According to a 25 January dispatch from Xinhua Wang, in 2006, Discipline Inspection and Supervision Units province-wide investigated 2,891 cases, punishing 3,009 persons, including 10 cadre at department level and 99 cadre at county (division) level, redeeming 200 million yuan in economic losses. They solved 242 commercial bribery cases, punishing 406 persons, involving 41.62 million yuan. These included the bribe-taking cases of Zhang Gaiping (1728 2395 5493), former Secretary of Shangzhou District Committee; Zhang Yongfu (1728 3057 4395), former Chairman of the Provincial Expressway Development Company; and Ouyang Fuqiang (2962 7122 1381 1730), former Party Secretary of the Provincial Wireless, Posts, and Telecommunications Bureau. [Guangzhou Dayang Wang (Internet Version-WWW) in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; http://china.dayoo.com/gb/content/2007-01/25/content_2744819.htm&nbsp;&nbsp; Baoji City Procuratorate Units Investigate 127 Government Officials in 2006 -- According to the 20 January issue of Xibu Fazhi Bao, in 2006, Baoji Procuratorate Units investigated 121 graft and bribery cases involving 127 persons, including 12 cadre at and above county (division) level, redeeming 7.28 million yuan in direct economic losses. They also captured seven fugitive corrupt officials. [Xian Xibu Fazhi Bao in Chinese -- Newspaper reporting on legal issues in Western China sponsored by the Shaanxi Province Politics and Law Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp; Shandong&nbsp;&nbsp; Former Provincial Economic and Trade Commission Vice Chairman Tried for Bribe-Taking -- According to a 29 January dispatch from Xinhua Wang, on 29 January 2007, Tai'an City Intermediate People's Court, tried Kong Fanli (1313 4907 4409), age 58, former Vice-Chairman of the Provincial Economic and Trade Commission, for accepting one million yuan in bribes. On 4 August 2006, Kong was arrested for bribe taking. From October 2002 to early 2006, Kong abused his power, sought benefits for others in the set up of a pawn broker business, import car quota allocations, and enterprise reforms, accepting 1.06 million yuan in bribes from 15 units and individuals. [Guangzhou Dayang Wang (Internet Version-WWW) in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; http://china.dayoo.com/gb/content/2007-01/29/content_2747845.htm&nbsp;&nbsp; Shanghai&nbsp;&nbsp; Shanghai Municipal Procuratorate Units Redeem 80 Million yuan in Economic Losses in 2006 -- According to the 23 January issue of Jiefang Ribao, Shanghai procuratorate units captured five fugitive officials, redeeming 83.03 million yuan in economic losses. They investigated 446 job-related cases, 495 persons, including 81 cadre at and above deputy division level. They solved 219 commercial bribery cases. [Shanghai Jiefang Ribao in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Sichuan&nbsp;&nbsp; Sichuan Provincial Procuratorate Units Investigate 19 Department Level Cadre in 2006 -- According to the 20 January issue of Sichuan Ribao, in 2006, procuratorate units investigated 1,736 job-related criminal cases involving 2,080 persons, including 189 cadre at county (division) level and 19 cadre at department level, redeeming 186 million yuan in economic losses. They investigated 632 commercial bribery cases involving 688 persons, including 105 cadre at and above county (division) level. [Chengdu Sichuan Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Sichuan Provincial CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Zhejiang&nbsp;&nbsp; Zhejiang Province Procuratorate Units Punish 117 Cadre at and above County (Division) Level in 2006 -- According to a 31 January dispatch from Xinhua Wang, in 2006, Procuratorate Units province-wide punished 110 cadre at county (division) level and 7 cadre at department level for job-related crimes. They investigated 1,214 graft, bribery, and dereliction of duty cases involving 1,445 persons, redeeming 175 million yuan in economic losses. [Guangzhou Dayang Wang (Internet Version-WWW) in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; http://china.dayoo.com/gb/content/2007-01/31/content_2749909.htm&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Organized Crimes/Triad Activities&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Henan&nbsp;&nbsp; Henan Province Police Smash 690 Criminal Syndicate-Like Organizations and Hooligan Gangs -- According to the 25 January issue of Henan Ribao, in 2006, Police Units province-wide smashed 690 criminal syndicate-like organization and hooligan gangs, capturing 23,471 Internet-wanted fugitives. [Zhengzhou Henan Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Henan Provincial CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp; Inner Mongolia&nbsp;&nbsp; Hohhot City Police Solve Criminal Syndicate-Like Organization Case -- According to the 25 January issue of Xinhua Meiri Dianxun, on 24 January 2007, E'erduosi Procuratorate initiated prosecution of nine police officials headed by Su He (5685 0735), Political Commissar of Tumd Left Banner PSB, and another criminal suspect for leading, organizing, and participating in criminal syndicate-like organization activities, committing rape, illegal hunting, illegal possession of guns, gambling, robbery, graft, embezzlement of public fund crimes, and possession of narcotics. Over the past ten years, Su, under a front company, Jin Yu Zhou Trading Limited Company [Jin Yu Zhou Company], engaged in criminal activities. The nine police officials included: He Changwei (0149 7022 0251), Secretary of the Discipline Inspection Committee; Yu Xinjiang (0060 2450 3068), Head of the Police Station on Quansheng Road; Nie Zilong (5119 1311 7893), former Commander of an Economic Police Unit; Heng Batu (1854 1572 0956), Head of Chasuqi Town Police Station; Zhang Junsheng (1728 0193 3932), Head of Bikeqi Town Police Station; Chen Jiping (7115 0679 1627), a civilian policeman of Bikeqi Town Police Station; Gao Yonggang (7559 3057 0474), a civilian policeman; and Ren Hongbiao (0117 4767 5753), a civilian policeman from a patrol police unit of Tumd Left Banner PSB. The procuratorate also prosecuted Kong Fanjun (1313 4907 6511), Vice President of Tumd Left Banner Jin Yu Zhou Company.[Beijing Xinhua Meiri Dianxun in Chinese]&nbsp;&nbsp; Ningxia&nbsp;&nbsp; Zhongwei City Urban District Court Tries 15 Criminal Syndicate-Like Organization Gangsters -- According to the 26 January issue of Ningxia Ribao, on 25 January 2007, the court tried 15 criminal syndicate-like organization gangsters headed by Bian Jingang (6708 6855 0474) for organizing, leading, and participating in criminal syndicate-like organization activities, and committing intentional injury, gambling, and rape crimes. Bian was sentenced to 13 years imprisonment. Since January 2001, Bian organized labor education released personnel and vagrants to operate casinos and collected debts. [Yinchuan Ningxia Ribao in Chinese -- daily newspaper of the Ningxia Hui Autonomous Region CPC Committee]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; THIS REPORT MAY CONTAIN COPYRIGHTED MATERIAL.&nbsp;&nbsp;COPYING AND DISSEMINATION IS PROHIBITED WITHOUT PERMISSION OF THE COPYRIGHT OWNERS.&nbsp;&nbsp;Inquiries regarding use may be directed to NTIS, US Dept. of Commerce; Publish Date: 20070207; Article ID: CPP20070206478001. Database Contributor: Media Africa. Database Contributor ID: 20070206478001. Language: Chinese. Accession Number: 20070206478001.</p>
