TY  - JOUR
TI  - RESOURCE UTILIZATION INDEXES - AN ASSESSMENT
AU  - LINTON, LR
AU  - DAVIES, RW
AU  - WRONA, FJ
T2  - JOURNAL OF ANIMAL ECOLOGY
AB  - The utility of 4 overlap indices was compared using computer sampled hypothetical utilization distributions. The amount of overlap between the distributions was progressively increased to unity; at each degree of overlap the sample size ranged from 10-320. The number of resource states ranged from 3-40. For all 4 indices plots of sample size vs. estimated overlap increased asymptotically, levelling out at a sample size of about 16 observations/resource. The results obtained by Pianka''s (1973) and Horn''s (1966) modification of Morisita''s (1959) indices were virtually identical. With renal overlaps between 7-85% only Schoener''s (1970) index estimated overlap accurately. Horn''s, Morisita''s and Pianka''s indices produced substantial misrepresentations of the data, even with large sample sizes. All 4 indices had similar accuracy in the 85-90% overlap range, but at higher overlaps Schoener''s index was least accurate. With overlaps of less than 7% Schoener''s and Horn''s indices were erratic and poor estimators of overlap, while Morisita''s and Pianka''s indices underestimated overlap by about 70%.
