AB  - Investigation of the background of 546 women prisoners shows that 18. 2% of their fathers died before the women were 15, and 13. 2% of the mothers, which is significantly higher than in the general population of this age group. Investigation of 168 male prisoners shows that 13. 4% of their fathers died before 15, and 8. 6% of their mothers. This is also significant. There is a high incidence of unknown parents in the women prisoners (14. 7%). Multiplicity of care and lack of stable parent figures in childhood are considered to be factors in both male and female criminality. The 546 women presoners had 366 children under 15. This gives them a social significance greater than their numbers alone would suggest.
