AB  - The proceedings contain 181 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Intelligent Systems. The topics include: Image Classification Method Considering Overlapping and Correlation Between Probability Density Functions of Features; 3D Reconstruction in Crime Scenes Investigation: Impacts, Benefits, and Limitations; a Hybrid Technique for English to Urdu Machine Translation Using Transfer Learning; a Cross Platform Mobile Application for Indoor Navigation; empowering Deaf Individuals: Ecuadorian Sign Language Dictionary Integration via Technology; New Integrations of Designers’ Solutions for Images in the VIS/NIR Spectral Area; towards Contextualizing Embodiment of Intelligent Systems; video Colorization Based on a Diffusion Model Implementation; improving Replenishment for Retail: Utilizing Planogram Information; evaluating and Improving Disparity Maps Without Ground Truth; JSTR: Judgment Improves Scene Text Recognition; effectiveness and Acceptance of Conversational Agent-Based Psychotherapy for Depression and Anxiety Treatment: Methodological Literature Review; Common Components Framework (CCF) Enabled Intelligent Data Processing; risk Assessment of Data Science Projects: A Literature Review on Risk Identification; exploring the Integration of Data Science Competencies in Modern Automation Frameworks: Insights for Workforce Empowerment; Enhanced MSME Support Allocation with Integrated K-means and Tukey's Outlier Detection; advancing Mortality Prediction in Ecuador Through Machine Learning Techniques; identification of Hidden Inheritance Patterns in a Relational Database Based on Ontologies; Predictive Analytics and AI-Driven Strategies for Enhanced Cash Flow Forecasting; embedding Inclusivity Design into the Data Science Curriculum; an Evaluation of Gender Bias in 167K Movie Posters; MDB: An Evaluative and Incentivizing Model Trading Market; On an Approximation Algorithm Combined with D3QN for HDFS Data Block Recovery in Heterogeneous Hadoop Clusters;