TI  - Mobile Forensics in Digital World using Artificial Intelligence
AU  - Dwivedi, A.
AU  - Singh, U.K.
AU  - Kathuria, S.
AU  - Lande, J.
AU  - Negi, P.
T2  - Proceedings - 2024 3rd International Conference on Sentiment Analysis and Deep Learning, ICSADL 2024
AB  - After the advent of industry 4.0, technologies are comprehensively unveiled to the public. Because of this, the proliferation in demand for technology in every field has begun to soar. Today, in the modern society, the pattern of crimes against women is increasing unprecedentedly. Cybercrimes are more frequent than traditional crimes. Therefore, Mobile Forensics (MF), a subset of digital forensics plays a crucial role in extracting the digital evidence. The technologies such as Artificial Intelligence (AI) is then incorporated to improve the efficiency and accuracy in mobile forensics and digital investigation. This study addresses the significance, challenges, and effects of integrating AI in Mobile Forensics and Digital Investigation (DI). In addition, this research study also emphasizes on the stages or directives of mobile forensics, which are considered as essential components in gathering the evidence. It fills the void by analyzing how various technologies and techniques such as machine learning, deep learning, and data mining can be used in mobile forensics. Eventually, this study is concluded by providing the suggestions for its advancement and avoidance while illustrating the challenges to negate the same in the future. © 2024 IEEE.
