TY  - JOUR
TI  - A collaborative policy-based security scheme to enforce resource access controlling mechanism
AU  - Muthumanickam, K.
AU  - Senthil Mahesh, P.C.
T2  - Wireless Networks
AB  - Advances in both telecommunications and Information technology have improved the way users do business online. Android, an open-source mobile operating system, is becoming an attractive target for cyber criminals to exploit due to its predefined permission model. Without classification, the mobile operating system permits installation of mobile applications of all kinds, including Trojans, thus making its trustworthiness into question. In this paper, we present a security system called collaborative policy-based security scheme (CSS) that permits users to customize the access permissions of Android applications during runtime. The proposed CSS security scheme validates the trustworthiness of each application before being installed. The experimental results show that the proposed CSS successfully detects all malicious applications with a run-time overhead of 2.7%. © 2019, Springer Science+Business Media, LLC, part of Springer Nature.
