AB  - Malicious activities in mobile applications may affect the mobile usages and even leave security concerns in the mobile applications. For example, they may drain the batteries, use up CPU or memories, increase bandwidth utilization, and even steal our information. In this paper, we analyze the Sherlock data to explore the patterns in mobile usage by different types of the mobile apps and their benign or malicious status. These initial findings potentially are helpful to assist malware detections and usage warning. © 2018 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
