TY  - BOOK
TI  - The art of defiance: graffiti, politics, and the reimagined city in Philadelphia
AU  - Mitman, Tyson
AB  - "The Art of Defiance is an ethnographic portrait of how graffiti writers see their city and, in turn, how their city sees them. It explores how becoming a graffiti writer helps disaffected urban citizens negotiate their cultural identities, build their social capital, and battle urban anomie. It also explains how graffiti, as a cultural practice, resists incorporation and commercialization while also granting practitioners a voice within an urban environment that would prefer them to remain quiet, passive, and anonymous. In order to both demystify and complicate our understanding of the practice of graffiti writing, this book pushes past the narrative that links the origins of graffiti to criminal gangs and instead offers a detailed portrait of graffiti as a rich urban culture with its own rules and practices. To do so, it examines the cultural history of graffiti in Philadelphia from the late 1960s onward and explores what it is like to be a graffiti writer in the city today. Ultimately, Tyson Mitman aims to humanize graffiti writers and to show that what they do is not merely destructive or puerile, but, rather, that it adds something important to the urban experience and is a conscious and deliberate act on the part of its practitioners to affect their city"--
